  "policyComment": "Native step-7 subset (McpTypedOpPolicy.decide). Native cannot verify the policy file seal (RN SecureStore) and cannot see RN cached policy, so it never clears an agent that declares ANY action: only an agent with no declared action is clearable (RN never refuses those at step 7 either). A deny rule {capability} the agents read-only actions have, in a policy file native can parse, refuses policy_denied (the safe direction). Everything else is undecidable: native treats it as no rule match (hand off to RN when RN is live, else not_attended). Changed after the Codex review 2026-11-15 (a deleted / replaced unsealed policy.json must not let native clear what RN cached policy denies).",
  "policyCases": [
    {
      "name": "no actions, any policy",
      "actions": [],
      "policy": {
        "kind": "shelly.user-policy",
        "userPolicy": {
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "p1",
              "effect": "deny",
              "match": {
                "capability": "exec"
              },
              "source": "test rule",
              "createdAt": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expected": "clearable"
    },
